117
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:03,107
OK, it's more than 95% correct.

118
00:08:03,107 --> 00:08:04,190
How do you think about it?

119
00:08:04,190 --> 00:08:04,981
What do I do first?

120
00:08:06,732 --> 00:08:09,510
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]

121
00:08:09,510 --> 00:08:11,120
DENNIS FREEMAN:
[INAUDIBLE] So what do

122
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,564
you want me to look at first?

123
00:08:12,564 --> 00:08:13,730
This diagram, that equation?

124
00:08:13,730 --> 00:08:14,896
This diagram, that equation?

125
00:08:14,896 --> 00:08:16,676
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]

126
00:08:16,676 --> 00:08:18,050
DENNIS FREEMAN:
Write an equation

127
00:08:18,050 --> 00:08:19,091
for each of the diagrams.

128
00:08:19,091 --> 00:08:22,016
How would I figure out an
